Prop Drilling (Without useContext) :-
Prop drilling is the process of passing data from a parent component to a deeply nested child component through multiple intermediate components using props, even when those intermediate components do not need to use the data themselves.

Scenario :-
We need to pass userName and eMailID from App to User through Dashboard and Profile.
we need to pass userName, eMailID as a prop through every component, even though Dashboard and Profile don't need to use it themselves.

Flow :-
App — owns userName, eMailID
        ↓ props
Dashboard — receives and passes props
        ↓ props
Profile — receives and passes props
        ↓ props
User — displays Name: aruntheja & Email: is aruntheja@gmail.com

How does it work :-
1. App creates the userName, eMailID are variable with the value "aruntheja", "aruntheja@gmail.com".
2. App passes them to Dashboard using userApp={userName} eMailApp={eMailID}.
3. Dashboard receives these props and passes them to Profile using userProfile={userDashboard} eMailProfile={eMailDashboard}.
4. Profile receives these props and passes them to User using ➡️ User - PropDrilling ➔ Name {userProfile} & Email is {eMailProfile}.
5. User displays as ➡️ User - PropDrilling ➔ Name: aruntheja & Email: is aruntheja@gmail.com.

Output :-
User - PropDrilling ➔ Name: aruntheja & Email: is aruntheja@gmail.com

Problem :- 
Dashboard and Profile only pass the data along without using it themselves. This is called Prop Drilling.

Solution :-
We can use React Context (useContext) to access shared data in deeply nested components without manually passing props through every intermediate component.
